&lt;p&gt;It keeps React’s programming model, but compiles Hooks, Suspense, and Actions ahead of time. It improves performance, removing the Virtual DOM and using native browser events. You don’t need to respect the rules of hooks or to maintain dependency arrays manually. You can use it with JSX/TSX, but it also supports &lt;a href="https://tsrx.dev/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;TSRX&lt;/a&gt; to improve your developer experience.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This looks like a quite serious React challenger using the same mental model, already receiving contributions from maintainers of popular project. It comes from day 1 with integrations for libraries such as TanStack, React Three Fiber, Lynx, StyleX, NativeScript, and more.&lt;/p&gt;




